928 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 648 0 R
/E (Schooling has a collective civic function that must be protected in the AI-era. Beyond individual skill development, schools provide shared references that sustain belonging, disagreement, and collective reasoning in communities. Much of this socialisation happens outside the syllabus, in the hidden curriculum of living, interacting, and making friends with peers from different backgrounds, and in a protected space where young people can raise complex, sometimes uncomfortable questions that may have no right answer. If digital pathways become too fragmented, especially through personalised learning, we risk weakening the common cultural and civic ground that social cohesion and democratic dialogue require.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
