970 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 650 0 R
/E (Throughout implementation, investments should be judged against all three purposes of education rather than learning gains alone: \(i\) qualification, by building knowledge and skills without encouraging dependence; \(ii\) socialisation, by maintaining shared learning experiences that foster community, debate and civic cohesion; and \(iii\) subjectification, by preserving human-in-the-loop educational relationships in which young people learn to think for themselves and answer for their choices.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
