1052 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 653 0 R
/E (iRAISE approaches digital literacy \(DL\) and AI literacy as skill sets critical for human agency: young people must be able to use digital tools without losing the relationships, agency, and critical thinking that underpin healthy development. Children increasingly encounter AI-generated content, AI-mediated social interactions, and AI-driven recommendation systems long before they can grasp how these systems work or where their limits lie \(Stoilova & Livingstone, 2025\). Still developing cognitively, emotionally, and socially, they may be particularly vulnerable to manipulation, surveillance, cognitive offloading, and emotional dependency \(Neugnot-Cerioli & Muss Laurenty, 2024\), even as GenAI holds promise for learning, creativity and personalised support \(UNICEF Innocenti, 2023\).)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
