1076 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 656 0 R
/E (This report is human-centred as our central assumption is that AI should augment, not replace, the relational, ethical, and motivational roles of teachers, caregivers, and peers. Any investment in DL and AI literacy must be judged by how well it strengthens human relationships and serves all three purposes, not qualification alone. International evidence points the same way: although AI systems can produce high-quality explanations and feedback, students perceive human feedback as more credible and meaningful, and more likely to influence their motivation, evaluative judgement and trust \(OECD, 2026a, ch. 1, p. 24\).)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
