/E (Overall, while this evidence base is still growing and remains uneven due to methodological limitations, results are indicative. Across these three domains, weaker DL is associated with lower academic achievement \(F. Li et al., 2025\), may leave children less able to cope with the online risks they encounter \(Livingstone et al., 2018\) and limit their ability to exercise rights that increasingly depend on digital access \(UNICEF, 2019\). This is why DL should be treated as foundational rather than supplementary in school curricula.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1113 0 obj
<<
