/P 659 0 R
/E (The next section examines why schools are the institution best placed to teach it to all children, and to do so effectively.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 659 0 R
/E (Schools are uniquely positioned to deliver structured, equitable DL and AI literacy education. Because DL and AI literacy sit at the crossroads of several policy agendas, schools are where these agendas meet children, which is why the education ministry is well placed to coordinate them. Schools play this role through four functions, each linked to one of these agendas: a distributive function \(connectivity and platform governance\), a pedagogical function \(curriculum and instruction\), a relational function \(child protection and wellbeing\), and a civic function \(democratic integrity\).)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
