/T (Designing effective DL and AI-Literacy policies requires robust assessment tools. However, existing digital-literacy instruments rely heavily on self-report questionnaires, have limited cross-cultural validation, and include few authentic performance assessments \(Suri et al., 2025\). AI-literacy instruments share these weaknesses and are rarely designed for children: of 16 validated scales identified in a systematic review, most target adults or university students, only three target secondary-school students. \(Lintner, 2024\). Additionally, none has been)
