/S /H1
/P 672 0 R
/T (Box 8. The recurring cost of localisation: Qatar, Egypt, and Canada )
/E (Box 8. The recurring cost of localisation: Qatar, Egypt, and Canada )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1274 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 672 0 R
/E (In Qatar, high-quality technical and AI materials remain scarcer in Arabic than in English, leaving schools and teachers with a heavy translation-and-adaptation workload. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1275 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 672 0 R
/E (Egypt has opted for curated, nationally hosted content: the Egyptian Knowledge Bank \(EKB\) has signed contracts with international publishers such as Britannica and Discovery Education to host verified, culturally adapted content, so that digital literacy is built on high-quality information rather than unverified open-web sources. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 672 0 R
/E (In Canada, digital-safety and media-literacy resources are plentiful but not always localised to cultural and linguistic contexts such as Francophone minority communities and newcomer families. )
/Pg 41 0 R
/K [9]
>>
