<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 678 0 R
/E (Across these four cases, a common pattern emerges when we examine what is working and what remains to be done. Effective DL education depends as much on human factors, such as teacher confidence, parental mediation and community trust, as on policy design.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1380 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 678 0 R
/E (While France has clear standards, there remain concerns around teacher uptake and implementation. Canada has a network of national NGOs with broad reported reach however there are challenges around country-wide coordination and national measurement of youth and teacher digital and AI literacy levels. Egypt has an impressive scale of initiatives however there remain considerations regarding technological adoption across generations and equipment gaps in primary and rural schools. Lastly, Qatar has abundant funding and infrastructure however there are issues around a digital-wellbeing paradox and needs DL and AI tools built on Arabic-language content and adapted to its cultural context.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
