/T (2. Training should be modular, ongoing and differentiated by role. What teachers need to know differs from what students need to learn, so teacher pathways should form a distinct programme that overlaps with, but does not duplicate, the student curriculum. Teachers who teach digital and AI literacy need in-depth preparation, whereas other subject teachers may need shorter, subject-specific training where GenAI is relevant to their discipline \(see Priority 1 in the Executive Summary\). Training should start in teacher education programmes at universities, so that all new teachers are prepared, and continue within paid working time.)
/E (2. Training should be modular, ongoing and differentiated by role. What teachers need to know differs from what students need to learn, so teacher pathways should form a distinct programme that overlaps with, but does not duplicate, the student curriculum. Teachers who teach digital and AI literacy need in-depth preparation, whereas other subject teachers may need shorter, subject-specific training where GenAI is relevant to their discipline \(see Priority 1 in the Executive Summary\). Training should start in teacher education programmes at universities, so that all new teachers are prepared, and continue within paid working time.)
