1506 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 685 0 R
/E (Few systems track how DL and AI literacy programmes are implemented or their long-term outcomes, and existing assessment instruments tend to emphasise technical skills over critical and ethical dimensions \(Sparks et al., 2024; Suri et al., 2025\). This measurement deficit is not merely an academic concern; without robust evidence on what works, governments risk investing in programmes that are popular but ineffective, or defunding ones that are effective but poorly documented.)
/Pg 54 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
1507 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 685 0 R
/E (Some countries, such as Estonia through its ProgeTiger programme, have built long-running national programmes that could support longitudinal follow-up of student outcomes. Emerging global assessments, including PISA 2029 MAIL, will provide complementary benchmarks, but they depend on countries having robust national data and classroom practices in place. Some AI providers have begun developing their own learning-outcome measures \(e.g., OpenAI, 2026\). Such efforts can add data, but evidence produced)
/Pg 54 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
