1511 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 686 0 R
/E (A practical corollary is that effective systems institutionalise continuous feedback from the people that DL is meant to serve. Regular structured surveys of caregivers, teachers, and students, rather than one-off evaluations, allow ministries and partners to detect emerging risks early, adapt content quickly, and keep programmes aligned with classroom realities. This feedback should also track implementation barriers and whether programmes are delivered as intended, since outcomes alone cannot reveal whether a programme is ineffective or poorly implemented. This agility matters because one of the most consistent challenges across contexts is that technology, especially GenAI, evolves faster than learning content and digital competencies of teachers, students, and caregivers. Common pitfalls include ignoring cultural context in assessment design, by assuming that Western frameworks apply universally, and failing to adapt )
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
