2241 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 714 0 R
/E (84% of primary, 87% of lower-secondary and 83% of upper-secondary schools had computers for teaching in 2023 \(Our World in Data, 2025\), although this indicator does not show how many devices are available per student. By late 2018, around 2,500 public general secondary schools had been connected to fibre to support tablet-based learning and assessment \(Reda, 2018; Zayed, 2025\), and the network has since been extended, although universal school connectivity remains a work in progress, particularly in rural areas \(Zayed, 2025\). Student logins are linked to national identifiers, enabling detailed tracking of engagement and performance via an Education Management Information System \(EMIS\). For a secondary-school student in Upper Egypt, this architecture means that, for the first time, she can access the same curated content as her peers in Cairo, using the same device, and sit the same standardized national exam. Yet it also means that her every interaction is logged from the age of fifteen, raising long-term questions about data protection, algorithmic bias, and student autonomy that the current governance framework has only begun to address.)
/Pg 83 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
