2261 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 716 0 R
/E (Working in partnership with MCIT and regional scouting movements, the Association plays a growing role in delivering online-safety and digital-citizenship workshops across Arab countries, including Egypt. Scouts act as trusted peer educators in their local communities, especially in rural and low-income areas where formal digital-literacy programmes are limited. The peer-education model is particularly well suited to contexts where institutional trust is low and parental resistance to digital reform is high: a young scout explaining data privacy to neighbours carries a different kind of credibility than a government leaflet. Co-creating AI-aware digital-safety tracks, designed to teach adolescents to recognise manipulation and misinformation, would extend this trusted channel to the most pressing emerging risks.)
/Pg 85 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
