<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 718 0 R
/E (The primary delivery mechanism is the Computing and Information Technology \(CIT\) curriculum, introduced in 2018 and taught as a separate subject from Grade 1 to Grade 12 \(MOEHE, 2018\). It is explicitly organised as a spiral curriculum in which concepts recur with increasing depth: pupils implement simple algorithms in a Logo environment in the early primary grades, move to block-based programming from Grade 4, and progress to text-based programming from Grade 9, alongside data modelling and relational databases \(MOEHE, 2018\).)
/Pg 87 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
2287 0 obj
<<
