/Title (strength of the association varies considerably by grade level, subject and gender, and the primary studies are correlational: DL and achievement go together, but this does not show that improving DL causes higher achievement. Access to technology may also confound the association, since students  with more access tend to have both stronger digital skills and more practice with digital tests, and since PISA has been computer-based since 2015. This is one reason why this report treats DL as both a skill in using tools and a broader understanding of how technology works. A systematic review of 31 studies. on digital tools in primary and secondary education)
